  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "New DIA, localization, de novo and glycan-repository tools and updated MIRAGE guidelines extend proteomics coverage from peptides to proteoforms and glycoproteomics.",
  "synthesis": "The items share an emphasis on extending proteomics beyond routine peptide identification toward proteoforms, modification site assignment, and glycan data. mE-DIA couples library-free multi-enzyme DIA with proteoform inference, reporting about 30% more protein IDs. onsite integrates alanine-decoy FLR estimation across AScore, PhosphoRS and pyLucXor for phosphosite localization. SeekNSee adds rule-based proteotypic peptide prioritization with enzyme-aware digestion, and CasanovoGUI lowers the barrier to Casanovo de novo sequencing. On the glycan side, GlycoPOST extends from glycomics to glycoproteomics under updated MIRAGE guidelines, while GlyTouCan v4 revises the glycan structure repository interface and API. The common thread is usability and standardized infrastructure rather than a single new method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
